MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "City of Evil fits my current interest in energetic metal with melodic riffs; I want heaviness that also gives me memorable guitar lines.",
    "The Sickness feels like a natural follow-up to Ten Thousand Fists, while We Are Not Alone connects with the melodic heaviness I enjoyed exploring through One Day Remains and The Reason."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "St. Anger feels off because its raw, repetitive sound does not offer the melodic detail I want right now, even though its heaviness looks relevant.",
    "Fallen interests me, but its melodic rock sound is lighter than what I would choose today. Several other albums fit my taste without being immediate choices on this visit."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seem to treat heavy guitars and aggression as enough to make an album appealing, when melody and engaging arrangements matter just as much to me.",
    "My interest in melodic rock seems to carry too much weight when it leads to gentler choices; right now I am leaning toward the heavier side of my listening."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent interest in 10.000 Days makes rhythmic complexity especially appealing, which helps explain why I would choose L.D. 50.",
    "There is a difference between an album fitting my general taste and making me want to listen now: City of Evil offers the melodic energy I currently want most."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understand my interest in heavy music, but sometimes miss the melody, rhythmic detail, and current listening mood that determine my choices."
}
